[00:08.73]1. Ev’ry newborn child, Ev’ry drop of rain,
[00:14.09]Ev’ry golden ray of sun, Each head of grain—
[00:21.29]All are gifts from God; They reveal his way.
[00:24.58]Miracles performed by him sustain us each day.
[00:27.86](Chorus)
[00:31.15]So, what are we to do with a gift so rare
[00:38.15]But to love the One who gave it and show him we care.
[00:49.15]No matter what we do, We never can earn it.
[00:53.66]This gift is still a gift—The miracle of life.
[01:12.76]2. Others may give up, Lose their will to try,
[01:18.76]Echoing the wife of Job: “Curse God and die.”
[01:25.76]We are not that way; Praise to God we give,
[01:35.56]Thanking him for ev’ry precious moment we live.
[01:37.91](Chorus)
[01:40.26]So, what are we to do with a gift so rare
[01:45.56]But to love the ones around us and show them we care.
[01:51.06]No matter what we do, We never can earn it.
[01:58.46]This gift is still a gift—The miracle of life.